{"id":"gp-25","slug":"gp-25","name":"GP-25 grenade launcher","aliases":["GP25","BG-15","GP-30","GP-34","VOG-25","VOG munition","GP-25"],"kind":"firearm","category":"firearms","subcategory":"Grenade launcher","description":"The GP-25 Kostyor (\"Bonfire\"), GP-30 Obuvka (\"Shoe\") and GP-34 are a family of Russian 40 mm under-barrel muzzleloaded grenade launchers for the AK family of assault rifles. The acronym GP stands for Granatomyot Podstvolnyj, \"under-barrel grenade launcher\" in Russian, and was adopted by Soviet forces in 1978.","development":"The development of a grenade launcher for the AKM assault rifle began in 1966 at the Central Design and Research Bureau of Sporting and Hunting Arms (TsKIB SOO). Development continued into the 1970s, and in 1978 it was accepted into service. The main production version was known as the GP-25, and could be attached to the AKM and AK-74 assault rifles. The GP-30 was made lighter and the aiming system was redesigned and moved to the right.\nGP grenade launchers are similar in appearance and fire the same Russian 40mm caliber ammunition. At the top of the barrel is the mounting hardware to attach the weapon to the underside of a rifle barrel, from which it is designed to fire. The GP barrel has a useful life of about 400 rounds.\nThe GP-30 first entered service in 1989, and is intended for use with the AK-100 series of assault rifles. The GP-30M is a grenade launcher of simplified model, consisting of a shorter 40 mm rifled barrel in front of a basic trigger mechanism with minimal hand grip.\nThe current Izhmash-made version, the GP-34, has a further-redesigned sighting system located to the right side of the weapon and features the following advantages:\nReliability: It is designed and tested specifically for the Kalashnikov assault rifles, fits such assault rifles directly without any adaptors or hand guard dismantling.\nImproved safety: The design prevents a round from moving within or falling out of the barrel, even if the muzzle is pointed down. The GP-34 features an additional mechanism (firing pin safety lever) to improve safety during loading.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"40 mm internal propellant caseless ammunition (CL)","numeric":40,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Action","value":"Closed system, single-shot"},{"label":"Rate of Fire","value":"20 rounds/min area suppression","numeric":20,"unit":"rounds/min"},{"label":"Rate of Fire","value":"5–6 rounds/min aimed shots"},{"label":"Muzzle Velocity","value":"76.5 m/s","numeric":76.5,"unit":"m/s"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"Muzzleloader"},{"label":"Sights","value":"Notched quadrant sight"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"1.5 kg (GP-25)","numeric":1.5,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"1.3 kg (GP-30)","numeric":1.3,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"1.4 kg (GP-34)","numeric":1.4,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Length","value":"323 mm (GP-25)","numeric":323,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Length","value":"275 mm (GP-30)","numeric":275,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Length","value":"315 mm (GP-34)","numeric":315,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"120 mm","numeric":120,"unit":"mm"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Effective Range","value":"Sights adjustable 100 to 400 meters"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"TsKIB SOO"},{"label":"Designed","value":"1966–1978"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Kalashnikov Concern"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"STC Delta"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Arsenal AD"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Zastava Arms"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1978–present"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"Soviet Union"},{"label":"In Service","value":"1978–present"}]}],"specIndex":{"Cartridge":"40 mm internal propellant caseless ammunition (CL)","Action":"Closed system, single-shot","Rate of Fire":"20 rounds/min area suppression","Muzzle Velocity":"76.5 m/s","Feed System":"Muzzleloader","Sights":"Notched quadrant sight","Weight":"1.5 kg (GP-25)","Length":"323 mm (GP-25)","Barrel Length":"120 mm","Effective Range":"Sights adjustable 100 to 400 meters","Designer":"TsKIB SOO","Designed":"1966–1978","Manufacturer":"Kalashnikov Concern","Produced":"1978–present","Origin":"Soviet Union","In Service":"1978–present"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Georgian_under_barrel_grenade_launchers_stc_delta_%283%29.JPG","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgian_under_barrel_grenade_launchers_stc_delta_(3).JPG","width":1604,"height":786,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Lynx-extra"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Georgian_under_barrel_grenade_launchers_stc_delta_%283%29.JPG/330px-Georgian_under_barrel_grenade_launchers_stc_delta_%283%29.JPG"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/%D0%AF%D0%BA_%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%82%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B8_%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%80%D1%83_%D1%96%D0%BC._%D0%A4%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8_%D1%83_%D0%9D%D0%B0%D1%86%D0%B3%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B4%D1%96%D1%97_%D1%82%D0%B0_%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%8F_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%85_6940_%2826939054060%29.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%AF%D0%BA_%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%82%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B8_%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%80%D1%83_%D1%96%D0%BC._%D0%A4%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B6%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8_%D1%83_%D0%9D%D0%B0%D1%86%D0%B3%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B4%D1%96%D1%97_%D1%82%D0%B0_%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%8F_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%85_6940_(26939054060).jpg","width":3861,"height":2574,"caption":"IMG_6940","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",